1
00:00:00,685 --> 00:00:03,315
(Penny:)So are you and Leonard working
on an experiment together?

2
00:00:03,480 --> 00:00:06,020
- Yeah, we are.
- We're examining the radiation levels...

3
00:00:06,191 --> 00:00:08,981
(Leonard:)...of photomultiplier tubes
for a new dark-matter detector.

4
00:00:09,152 --> 00:00:11,782
(Penny:)Sweetie, sweetie, Dave was talking.

5
00:00:12,364 --> 00:00:14,154
(Penny:)You know, I love science.

6
00:00:14,324 --> 00:00:16,534
- Since when?
- Since always.

7
00:00:16,993 --> 00:00:21,623
(Penny:)Call me a geek, but I am just nuts
for the whole subatomic-particle thing.

8
00:00:21,790 --> 00:00:24,380
DAVID: The last thing
I would ever call you is a geek.

9
00:00:24,543 --> 00:00:28,173
Oh, well, that's what I am.
Queen of the nerds.

10
00:00:28,338 --> 00:00:31,218
Hey, if you'd like, I could show you
the lab we're working in.

11
00:00:31,383 --> 00:00:33,883
(David:)We've got some cool toys, you know.
Lasers and stuff.

12
00:00:34,052 --> 00:00:37,432
(Penny:)You know, I have always wanted to see
a big science lab.

13
00:00:37,597 --> 00:00:40,137
- Since when?
- Since always.

14
00:00:40,308 --> 00:00:41,808
(David:)Leonard, are you okay here?

15
00:00:41,977 --> 00:00:44,057
(Leonard:)- Yeah, I guess.
- How about we go see it now?

16
00:00:44,229 --> 00:00:47,399
(David:)Afterwards, we take the bike up the coast,
we grab a bite to eat?

17
00:00:47,566 --> 00:00:51,446
Um, yeah. Yeah, that sounds great.
Let me just get my jacket.

18
00:00:53,655 --> 00:00:54,825
[DOOR CLOSES]

19
00:00:54,990 --> 00:00:57,070
(David:)Boy, she'll do, huh?

20
00:00:58,285 --> 00:01:00,705
(Leonard:)Yeah, if you like that type.

